---
title: Sous Vide Thick Lamb Chops
servings: 4
tags: CSO, Sous Vide, AI
source.author: AI Cooking Agent
course: Main dish
prep time: 12 hours
cook time: 2.5 hours
difficulty: Moderate
---

= Pre-Season =

> Regardless of cooking method, pre-season and dry brine the meat overnight.

Start the dry brine ~{12-24%hours} ahead of cooking.

Lightly score the fat cap, making sure not to cut into the meat.

Mix @kosher salt{} (enough to generously coat the meat), @black pepper{}, @rosemary{}(fresh), and @thyme{}(fresh) in a small bowl.
Rub the mixture over all sides of the meat.

Place the chops on a wire rack over a pan or plate and place in the refrigerator, uncovered, overnight.

> Rosemary and Thyme are a classic pairing with lamb. The salt deeply penetrates the meat for better seasoning and moisture retention.

= Method 1: Sous Vide or CSO =

> This can be done with a sous vide water bath, or using basically the same process in a Convection Steam Oven (CSO).

Start a #sous vide cooker{} with a water bath, or start a #convection steam oven{} in sous vide or steam mode at 131°F (for medium doneness).

Transfer the chops with the seasonings to one or more #vacuum bags{}. 
Add @butter{1/2%Tbsp}(unsalted) and @garlic{1%tsp}(minced or crushed) per lamb chop to each bag, then seal with a #vacuum sealer{}.

Cook for ~{2-2.5%hours}.

When done cooking, remove from the water bath. Continue to the Final Sear steps below.

= Method 2: Convection Steam Roast =

> Faster than the sous vide water bath, the convection steam mode improves heat transfer and prevents drying compared to dry ovens.

Remove the chops from the refrigerator and place on a perforated pan.

Place a modular (2-tier) rack in the #convection steam oven{} on the 2nd lowest position. 
Place a solid pan in the bottom tray of the modular rack.
Preheat the oven in convection steam mode at 325°F.

If equipped, place an oven probe into the thickest chop. 
Place the perforated pan on top of the modular rack and cook for ~{15-30%minutes} (depending on thickness) until the internal temperature reaches 125-128°F.

When the temperature has been reached, remove from the oven. Continue to the Final Sear steps below.

= Method 3: Convection Bake =

> If you are not equipped with a Sous Vide cooker or CSO, you can still get solid performance from a convection oven.

Remove the chops from the refrigerator ~{30%minutes} prior to cooking.
Place the chops on a wire rack over a baking pan.

Preheat the oven on convection mode or convection bake at 250°F.

Cook the chops for ~{15-30%minutes} (depending on thickness) until the internal temperature reaches 125-128°F.

When the temperature has been reached, remove from the oven. Continue to the Final Sear steps below.

= All Methods: Final Sear =

Remove the chops from the bags or from the oven and wipe off any excess herbs.
Thoroughly pat the chops dry and set aside for ~{5%minutes}.

Heat a #cast iron pan{} over high heat (target 500°F with an infrared surface thermometer).
After reaching temperature, add @grapeseed oil{2%Tbsp}(or other high smoke point oil) and coat the pan.
Sear the chops for ~{60-90%seconds} on each side.

Target a final internal temperature of 135°F for a perfect medium cook, or 140°F for more doneness.

At the end of the sear, remove from the heat. Optionally baste with prepared @garlic butter{}.

= Final Serving (All Methods) =

@./Side Dishes/Chimichurri Sauce{}(optional) is a great accompaniment to spoon over the lamb. 
Spoon a ribbon of the sauce over the meat but do not cover fully.

Serve with @./Convection Steam Oven/CSO Fingerling Potatoes{}(optional) and/or @./Convection Steam Oven/Garlic-Confit Green Beans{}(optional) as side dishes.
